Reload a page that stops answering, in place

Once a page has finished loading, ask it a trivial question every 5 s. If a
question goes unanswered for SURF_PAGE_DEADLINE seconds, terminate the page's
web process and load the launch URI in a fresh one. The browser and the X
server keep running.

Off unless SURF_PAGE_DEADLINE is a positive integer, the same opt-in style as
the variables in 0001.

This is C inside surf's main loop and signal handlers, so it cannot be a
bbappend change.

Applies after 0001-kiosk-milestones-and-override-redirect.patch.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [kiosk-specific]
